Bolivian soldiers and the country's  indigenous people welcomed Pope Francis  at el alto airport he was joined by  President Evo Morales who held his fist  in the air in a salute the Pope then  traveled on to the capital lapaz where  he addressed the crowds outside the  presidential palace the pontiff chose to  visit three of South America's poorest  countries Ecuador Bolivia and Paraguay  to raise awareness of dire poverty  levels in the region the city Cathedral  turned into a sea of cell phones as the  pontiff made his way to the altar the  congregation clamored to take a  photograph of the continents first pope  after lapaz the Pope flew to Santa Cruz  where he began his whistle stop tour he  addressed the issue of integrating  different ethnic groups in the socialist  country Bolivia estudando pesos in  Bolivia is making important steps  towards including broad sectors in the  country's economic social and political  life your Constitution recognizes the  rights of individuals minorities and the  natural environment followers even slept  on the streets to catch a glimpse of  Francis on his so-called homecoming tour  you
 

